Content-Type: application/json
X-API-KEY: Tas-Man-Sys-ApiKey-Vince-Backup-524

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### GET TASKS - PASTE EMPLOYEE, MANAGER, OR ADMIN TOKEN
GET {{Task_Management_System_HostAddress}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{paste-token-name}}

### CREATE TASK - PASTE ADMIN OR MANAGER TOKEN
POST {{Task_Management_System_HostAddress}}/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{paste-token-name}}

{
  "title": "Finish Documentation",
  "description": "Complete the API documentation"
}

### UPDATE TASK - PASTE ADMIN OR MANAGER TOKEN
PUT {{Task_Management_System_HostAddress}}/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{paste-token-name}}

{
  "title": "Prepare Report Updated",
  "description": "Update and finalize weekly report",
  "status": "Completed"
}

### GET USERS - ADMIN ONLY
GET {{Task_Management_System_HostAddress}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### DELETE USER - ADMIN ONLY 
DELETE {{Task_Management_System_HostAddress}}/api/admin/users/3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}



### So how was I able to make it work? I simply just needed to change the address into a https one
### to do that check for the output window and check for listening on and copy the https address
### I was not properly able to test if it was working before because I can't get past the 
### unauthorized error due to the http address. 
### it errors on http because http, from my understanding, drops the JWT token in the header thus making
### every request unauthenticated and thus unauthorized.
### With some changes here and there from the development branch, it now works.